---
// Flagship A — page anatomy per spec §A5.
// Dark-first, data-case="nightlights" identity (spec §A6).
import "../styles/tokens.css";
import "maplibre-gl/dist/maplibre-gl.css";
import summary from "../data/summary.json";

const vintage = summary.latestMonth;
const javaPct = Math.round(summary.javaShareSOL * 100);
const landPct = (summary.javaLandShare * 100).toFixed(1);
const maxSol = summary.topSol[0].v;
const maxMean = summary.topMean[0].v;
---
<html lang="en" data-case="nightlights" data-theme="dark">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>Nighttime-Lights Economic Pulse</title>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Archivo:wght@500;600;700&family=Public+Sans:wght@400;500;600&family=IBM+Plex+Mono:wght@400;500;600&display=swap" />
  </head>
  <body>

    <header class="stamp-bar">
      <span class="stamp">NIGHTTIME-LIGHTS ECONOMIC PULSE</span>
      <span class="stamp dim">DATA THROUGH {vintage} · {summary.monthCount} MONTHS · NASA BLACK MARBLE</span>
    </header>

    <section class="hero">
      <img id="hero-still" src={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, "")}/hero.jpg`}
           alt={`Indonesia at night, ${vintage} — NASA Black Marble radiance rendered in amber`} />
      <div class="frames" id="hero-frames" hidden aria-hidden="true">
        <img class="f a" alt="" /><img class="f b" alt="" />
      </div>
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <h1>From 830&nbsp;km up, Indonesia looks like this.</h1>
        <p>Every year since 2012, every month since 2018: satellite radiance
        translated into a regency-level map of economic activity, refreshed monthly
        against regional accounts that arrive once a year.</p>
        <span class="stamp dim" id="hero-prod">VJ146A3 · {vintage} · 15 ARC-SECOND COMPOSITE</span>
      </div>
      <div class="year-hud" id="hero-hud" hidden aria-live="off">
        <span class="year" id="hero-year"></span>
        <span class="stamp dim">ANNUAL COMPOSITES · ONE FIXED STRETCH</span>
      </div>
      <div class="year-bar" id="hero-bar" hidden aria-label="year"><b></b></div>
      <div class="scroll-hint" aria-hidden="true">▾</div>
    </section>

    <section class="chapter">
      <span class="eyebrow">01 · Concentration</span>
      <h2>Java carries the light</h2>
      <p class="big-stat"><b class="amber">{javaPct}%</b> of Indonesia’s night light
      comes from <b class="amber">{landPct}%</b> of its land.</p>
      <div class="share-bars" role="img" aria-label={`Java: ${javaPct}% of lights, ${landPct}% of land`}>
        <div class="share-row"><span class="stamp dim">LIGHT</span><div class="bar"><i style={`width:${javaPct}%`}></i></div></div>
        <div class="share-row"><span class="stamp dim">LAND</span><div class="bar"><i style={`width:${landPct}%`}></i></div></div>
      </div>
      <p>One island holds the archipelago’s economic gravity. Every regency’s share
      of that light — and how it moves month to month — is measurable from orbit.
      That is what this instrument does.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="chapter">
      <span class="eyebrow">02 · The pulse</span>
      <h2>The series so far</h2>
      <p>National sum of lights per month, 2018 to the latest composite; the
      ledger grows by one month each time NASA publishes. Hollow points mark
      monsoon months, where cloud cover leaves few clear observations — the
      pipeline reports what it cannot see rather than guessing. Press play on the
      map below to watch every regency move.</p>
      <div id="pulse-chart" class="chart"></div>
      <p class="footnote">Values are lights-implied activity, not GDP. The coverage-weighted,
      seasonally adjusted version of this series meets BPS’s regional accounts in chapter 04.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="chapter">
      <span class="eyebrow">03 · Where</span>
      <h2>Where the light is · {vintage}</h2>
      <div class="top-lists">
        <div>
          <h3 class="stamp">TOTAL LIGHT — BREADTH</h3>
          <ol class="ranked">
            {summary.topSol.map((r) => (
              <li><span class="rname">{r.name}</span>
                  <span class="rbar"><i style={`width:${(r.v / maxSol) * 100}%`}></i></span>
                  <span class="rval">{r.v.toLocaleString()}</span></li>
            ))}
          </ol>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="stamp">MEAN RADIANCE — INTENSITY</h3>
          <ol class="ranked">
            {summary.topMean.map((r) => (
              <li><span class="rname">{r.name}</span>
                  <span class="rbar"><i style={`width:${(r.v / maxMean) * 100}%`}></i></span>
                  <span class="rval">{r.v}</span></li>
            ))}
          </ol>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p>Breadth and intensity tell different stories: industrial Bekasi and Bogor
      lead on total light, while Jakarta’s dense urban cores lead on brightness per
      pixel. (Kutai Kartanegara’s total is inflated by gas flaring — chapter 04
      shows the flare mask that corrects for it.)</p>
    </section>

    <section class="chapter wide calib" id="calibration">
      <span class="eyebrow">04 · Calibration</span>
      <h2>The instrument, calibrated</h2>
      <p>Do the lights actually track the economy? Here the index meets BPS’s
      regional accounts: real PDRB for all 514 regencies — annual and quarterly.
      The verdict is two-sided, and both sides are printed. <b>Where</b> activity
      is, lights explain about 70% of the cross-regency variation, every year
      (the location check). <b>When</b> it moves, the short-run link is too weak to use: the
      growth coefficient’s interval contains zero, and out of sample the mapping
      loses to simply assuming last year’s growth. 2020 is usually offered as the
      proof case; on our own numbers it is not one — lights fell 2.1% and GDP fell
      2.1%, but satellite coverage collapsed that year too, so signal and artefact
      cannot be separated. The uncertainty bands below are that sentence, drawn.</p>

      <div class="tiles" id="calib-tiles" hidden>
        <div class="tile"><span class="t-label">Where · levels fit</span>
          <span class="t-value" id="t-gate-v">—</span>
          <span class="t-sub" id="t-gate-s"></span></div>
        <div class="tile"><span class="t-label">Elasticity (within regency)</span>
          <span class="t-value" id="t-el-v">—</span>
          <span class="t-sub" id="t-el-s"></span></div>
        <div class="tile"><span class="t-label">When · short-run growth link</span>
          <span class="t-value" id="t-gr-v">—</span>
          <span class="t-sub" id="t-gr-s"></span></div>
        <div class="tile"><span class="t-label">Growth nowcast · withdrawn</span>
          <span class="t-value amber" id="t-nc-v">—</span>
          <span class="t-sub" id="t-nc-s"></span></div>
      </div>

      <div class="calib-block" id="calib-pulse-block" hidden>
        <h3 class="stamp">LIGHTS-IMPLIED ACTIVITY VS OFFICIAL GROWTH · YEAR-ON-YEAR</h3>
        <div class="chart-legend" aria-hidden="true">
          <span class="key"><i class="k-line" style="border-color:#E8A33D"></i>LIGHTS-IMPLIED ACTIVITY (3-MO WINDOW)</span>
          <span class="key"><i class="k-band" style="background:#E8A33D"></i>95% BAND</span>
          <span class="key"><i class="k-line" style="border-color:#4BB8A9"></i>BPS REAL PDRB · ANNUAL</span>
          <span class="key"><i class="k-dot" style="background:#4BB8A9"></i>BPS QUARTERLY (YOY)</span>
        </div>
        <div id="calib-pulse" class="chart"></div>
        <p class="footnote" id="calib-pulse-note">Lights-implied growth = the quarterly growth calibration
        (a + β·Δlog lights) applied to the deseasonalised national series; the band is a 95% interval from the
        calibration’s parameter and residual uncertainty. It is an <b>activity index, never GDP</b>. The shaded
        zone is the nowcast — months where BPS has not yet published.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="calib-block" id="calib-scatter-block" hidden>
        <h3 class="stamp">LOCATION CHECK · LOG REAL PDRB ~ LOG LIGHTS, ONE DOT PER REGENCY <span class="gate-chip" id="sc-gate"></span></h3>
        <div class="controls" style="flex-wrap:wrap; justify-content:flex-start; gap:10px;">
          <div class="toggle sc-years" id="sc-years" role="group" aria-label="calibration year"></div>
          <span class="stamp dim" id="sc-r2"></span>
        </div>
        <div class="scatter-row">
          <div id="calib-scatter" class="chart"></div>
          <div class="weak-list">
            <h4 class="stamp dim" style="margin:0" id="wk-title">WHERE SATELLITE AND STATISTICS DISAGREE</h4>
            <ol id="calib-weak"></ol>
            <p class="footnote">Largest standardised residuals in the latest BPS year. A regency that is
            bright but poor, or dark but rich, is one where the satellite and the statistical office tell
            different stories — a question worth asking, and the most useful thing this instrument
            produces. Hollow dots on the scatter are flare-corrected oil &amp; gas regencies.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="calib-block" id="calib-flares-block" hidden>
        <h3 class="stamp">FLARES REMOVED BEFORE ANY OF THIS</h3>
        <p class="footnote" id="calib-flares-note"></p>
        <ol class="ranked" id="calib-flares"></ol>
        <p class="footnote" id="calib-flares-src"></p>
      </div>

      <p class="footnote" id="calib-pending">Calibration data hasn’t published yet — this chapter fills in
      when the model stage lands on the server.</p>
      <div id="calib-tip" hidden></div>
    </section>

    <section class="explore">
      <div class="explore-head">
        <span class="eyebrow">05 · Explore</span>
        <h2>Every regency, every month</h2>
        <div class="controls">
          <label class="stamp dim">MONTH
            <select id="month-select"></select>
          </label>
          <div class="toggle" role="group" aria-label="metric">
            <button id="btn-sol" class="on">TOTAL LIGHT</button><button id="btn-mean">INTENSITY</button>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="how-to-read"><b>Total light</b> is the sum of radiance falling inside a regency, so it
        rewards size and breadth — big industrial regencies lead. <b>Intensity</b> is the mean radiance
        per pixel, which is independent of size — dense city cores lead. Darker means dimmer, on a log
        scale that is <b>fixed across all 103 months</b>, so colours are comparable as the player runs.
        One consequence is worth knowing before you read the animation: a cloudy monsoon month goes dark
        across the whole map because the satellite saw less of it, not because the lights went out. The
        coverage figure below the slider tells you which months those are.</p>
      </div>
      <div id="map"></div>
      <div class="map-foot">
        <div class="legend" id="legend" aria-hidden="true">
          <span class="stamp dim" id="legend-title">TOTAL LIGHT</span>
          <div class="legend-ramp"><i></i></div>
          <div class="legend-ticks" id="legend-ticks"></div>
          <span class="legend-note stamp dim">log scale · fixed across all months · top 0.5% clipped</span>
        </div>
        <div class="player" aria-label="month player">
          <button id="btn-play" aria-label="play">▶</button>
          <input id="month-range" type="range" min="0" max="0" step="1" value="0" aria-label="month" />
          <output class="month-out" id="hud-month"></output>
          <div class="hud"><span id="hud-sol"></span><span id="hud-cov"></span><span id="hud-mover"></span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <aside id="region-panel" hidden>
        <button id="panel-close" aria-label="close">×</button>
        <h3 id="panel-name"></h3>
        <div class="stamp dim" id="panel-bps"></div>
        <dl class="panel-stats">
          <dt>SUM OF LIGHTS</dt><dd id="panel-sol"></dd>
          <dt>MEAN RADIANCE</dt><dd id="panel-mean"></dd>
        </dl>
        <div id="panel-spark"></div>
        <div class="stamp dim" id="panel-months"></div>
      </aside>
      <div id="tooltip" hidden></div>
    </section>
    <div id="chart-tip" hidden></div>

    <section class="chapter review-cta">
      <span class="eyebrow">06 · Review</span>
      <h2>We had this instrument reviewed, adversarially.</h2>
      <p>An independent read of the same data against the published literature. It replicates Gibson
      et al. (2021) on Indonesian kabupaten and finds their rural verdict is a property of the sensor
      product, not of night lights; it explains why the growth nowcast has been withdrawn; and it
      corrects a claim this page used to make about 2020.</p>
      <a class="cta big" href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, "")}/article`}>Read the review article →</a>
    </section>

    <footer class="method">
      <span class="eyebrow">Methodology & sources</span>
      <p>Radiance: NASA Black Marble VJ146A3 monthly composites (Román et al. 2018),
      NOAA-20 VIIRS, 15 arc-second, QA-masked at &lt;2 cloud-free observations.
      Boundaries: geoBoundaries gbOpen IDN ADM2 (CC BY 3.0 IGO), 2020 vintage, frozen.
      Regional statistics: exact area-weighted extraction, 514 regencies matched 1:1
      to BPS codes. Hero timelapse: annual composites VNP46A4 (Suomi-NPP, 2012–2017)
      and VJ146A4 (NOAA-20, 2018→), every year rendered with the same fixed log stretch
      (ceiling 30 nW/cm²·sr, block-max downsampling) — the two sensors are
      cross-calibrated by NASA but not identical, so read the years, not the brightness.
      <b>This index measures light, not GDP</b> — chapter 04 publishes the calibration against
      BPS regional accounts (real PDRB ADHK per kabupaten/kota, BPS WebAPI: annual table 2194,
      quarterly table 2534) with its full fit statistics, including where the fit is weak.
      Seasonal adjustment is coverage-weighted (monsoon months carry little weight) with a
      Ramadan-overlap regressor on the Hijri calendar. Gas flares are masked with 3&nbsp;km
      buffers around persistent sites from the VIIRS Nightfire global flare survey 2012–2019
      (Elvidge &amp; Zhizhin 2021, ORNL DAAC, doi:10.3334/ORNLDAAC/1874, openly shared without
      restriction); the raw series is kept alongside.</p>
      <span class="stamp dim">A DEMO-LAB CASE · PIPELINE RERUNS MONTHLY · GENERATED {vintage}</span>
    </footer>

    <script>
      import maplibregl from "maplibre-gl";
      import * as d3 from "d3";

      /* visible failure beats silent emptiness (same pattern as the trade page) */
      const failBanner = (msg) => {
        let b = document.getElementById("err-banner");
        if (!b) {
          b = document.createElement("div"); b.id = "err-banner";
          b.style.cssText = "position:fixed;bottom:0;left:0;right:0;z-index:99;background:#3A1E1A;color:#F26D5B;font:12px ui-monospace,monospace;padding:10px 16px;border-top:1px solid #F26D5B;";
          document.body.appendChild(b);
        }
        b.textContent = "⚠ " + msg;
      };
      addEventListener("error", (e) => failBanner("Script error: " + (e.message ?? e.type)));
      addEventListener("unhandledrejection", (e) => failBanner("Load error: " + (e.reason?.message ?? e.reason)));
      const sect = (name, fn) => { try { return fn(); } catch (err) { console.error(name, err); failBanner(`${name} failed: ${err.message ?? err}`); return null; } };

      const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, "");
      const RAMP = ["#05070F", "#1B2447", "#7A5A22", "#E8A33D", "#FFEFC9"];
      const state = { month: null, metric: "sol", region: null };

      /* ---------- hero: annual timelapse (frames from pipeline/frames.py; the still stands if absent) ---------- */
      heroTimelapse().catch((e) => console.warn("hero timelapse unavailable:", e?.message ?? e));
      async function heroTimelapse() {
        const res = await fetch(`${base}/frames/index.json`);
        if (!res.ok) return;
        const frames = (await res.json()).years;
        if (frames.length < 2) return;
        const wrap = document.getElementById("hero-frames"), still = document.getElementById("hero-still");
        const imgs = [wrap.querySelector("img.a"), wrap.querySelector("img.b")];
        const hudEl = document.getElementById("hero-hud"), yearEl = document.getElementById("hero-year");
        const prodEl = document.getElementById("hero-prod");
        const bar = document.getElementById("hero-bar"), fill = bar.querySelector("b");
        const load = (f) => new Promise((ok, no) => {
          const im = new Image(); im.onload = () => ok(im.src); im.onerror = () => no(new Error(`frame ${f.file}`));
          im.src = `${base}/frames/${f.file}`;
        });
        const srcs = new Array(frames.length);
        srcs[0] = await load(frames[0]);
        frames.forEach((f, i) => {
          const t = document.createElement("i");
          t.style.left = `${(i / (frames.length - 1)) * 100}%`; t.title = String(f.year);
          t.onclick = () => { clearTimeout(timer); show(i).then(schedule); };
          bar.appendChild(t);
        });
        const reduced = matchMedia("(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)").matches;
        let cur = 0, flip = 0, timer = null;
        async function show(i) {
          if (!srcs[i]) srcs[i] = await load(frames[i]);
          cur = i; flip ^= 1;
          imgs[flip].src = srcs[i];
          imgs[flip].classList.add("on"); imgs[flip ^ 1].classList.remove("on");
          yearEl.textContent = frames[i].year;
          prodEl.textContent = `${frames[i].product} · ${frames[i].year} · ANNUAL 15 ARC-SECOND COMPOSITE`;
          fill.style.width = `${(i / (frames.length - 1)) * 100}%`;
        }
        function schedule() {
          if (reduced) return;
          const last = cur === frames.length - 1;
          timer = setTimeout(() => show(last ? 0 : cur + 1).then(schedule).catch(() => {}), last ? 3400 : 1400);
        }
        wrap.hidden = false; hudEl.hidden = false; bar.hidden = false;
        await show(reduced ? frames.length - 1 : 0);
        setTimeout(() => { still.hidden = true; }, 900);
        (async () => { for (let i = 1; i < frames.length; i++) if (!srcs[i]) srcs[i] = await load(frames[i]).catch(() => null); })();
        schedule();
      }

      const [geo, ledger] = await Promise.all([
        fetch(`${base}/data/regencies.geojson`).then((r) => r.json()),
        fetch(`${base}/data/ledger.json`).then((r) => r.json()),
      ]);
      state.month = ledger.months[ledger.months.length - 1];
      // populate the month control immediately — it must not depend on the map's fate
      {
        const sel0 = document.getElementById("month-select");
        for (const m of ledger.months) sel0.add(new Option(m, m));
        sel0.value = state.month;
      }

      /* national series — shared by the pulse chart and the month-player HUD */
      const national = ledger.months.map((m) => {
        let sol = 0, px = 0;
        for (const id in ledger.regions) {
          const s = ledger.regions[id].series[m];
          if (s) { sol += s[0]; px += s[2]; }
        }
        return { m, sol, px };
      });
      const peakPx = d3.max(national, (d) => d.px);
      const regionPeakPx = {};
      for (const id in ledger.regions)
        regionPeakPx[id] = d3.max(Object.values(ledger.regions[id].series), (s) => s[2]) || 1;

      /* ---------- chapter 2: national pulse ---------- */
      {
        const el = document.getElementById("pulse-chart");
        const W = el.clientWidth, H = 260, M = { t: 16, r: 16, b: 28, l: 64 };
        const series = national, peak = peakPx;
        const x = d3.scalePoint(series.map((d) => d.m), [M.l, W - M.r]).padding(0.5);
        const y = d3.scaleLinear([0, d3.max(series, (d) => d.sol) * 1.1], [H - M.b, M.t]);
        const svg = d3.select(el).append("svg").attr("width", W).attr("height", H);
        svg.append("g").attr("transform", `translate(${M.l},0)`)
          .call(d3.axisLeft(y).ticks(4).tickFormat(d3.format("~s"))).attr("class", "axis");
        svg.append("g").attr("transform", `translate(0,${H - M.b})`)
          .call(d3.axisBottom(x)
            .tickValues(series.map((d) => d.m).filter((m) => m.endsWith("-01")))
            .tickFormat((m) => m.slice(0, 4)))
          .attr("class", "axis");
        svg.append("path").datum(series)
          .attr("d", d3.line().x((d) => x(d.m)).y((d) => y(d.sol)))
          .attr("fill", "none").attr("stroke", "#E8A33D").attr("stroke-width", 1.5)
          .attr("stroke-dasharray", series.length < 6 ? "2 4" : null);
        const dots = svg.selectAll("circle").data(series).join("circle")
          .attr("cx", (d) => x(d.m)).attr("cy", (d) => y(d.sol)).attr("r", 3.5)
          .attr("fill", (d) => (d.px / peak < 0.5 ? "transparent" : "#E8A33D"))
          .attr("stroke", "#E8A33D").attr("stroke-width", 1.4);
        // hover: crosshair + tooltip (coverage explains the hollow months)
        const ctip = document.getElementById("chart-tip");
        const guide = svg.append("line").attr("y1", M.t).attr("y2", H - M.b).attr("stroke", "#E9E4D6").attr("stroke-opacity", 0.4).style("display", "none");
        svg.append("rect").attr("x", M.l).attr("y", M.t).attr("width", W - M.l - M.r).attr("height", H - M.t - M.b).attr("fill", "transparent")
          .on("mousemove", (e) => {
            const px = d3.pointer(e)[0];
            const d = series.reduce((best, s) => (Math.abs(x(s.m) - px) < Math.abs(x(best.m) - px) ? s : best), series[0]);
            guide.style("display", null).attr("x1", x(d.m)).attr("x2", x(d.m));
            dots.attr("r", (s) => (s === d ? 6 : 3.5));
            ctip.hidden = false; ctip.style.left = e.pageX + 14 + "px"; ctip.style.top = e.pageY + 14 + "px";
            ctip.innerHTML = `<b>${d.m}</b><br>sum of lights ${d3.format(",.0f")(d.sol)}<br>coverage ${d3.format(".0%")(d.px / peak)}${d.px / peak < 0.5 ? " — <span style='color:#6B7CA6'>monsoon-masked, low confidence</span>" : ""}`;
          })
          .on("mouseleave", () => { guide.style("display", "none"); dots.attr("r", 5); ctip.hidden = true; });
      }

      /* ---------- explore: choropleth (WebGL map · 2-D canvas fallback) ---------- */
      const values = (month, metric) => {
        const idx = metric === "sol" ? 0 : 1;
        const out = new Map();
        for (const id in ledger.regions) {
          const s = ledger.regions[id].series[month];
          if (s) out.set(id, s[idx]);
        }
        return out;
      };
      /* ONE fixed scale per metric, taken over every month at once. Re-deriving the
         ceiling from each month's own distribution (as this did) made colours mean
         different things in different frames, so the player animated the shifting
         distribution as if it were shifting light — the same trap frames.py avoids
         in the hero with a single fixed stretch. */
      const scaleCache = {};
      const scaleFor = (metric) => {
        if (scaleCache[metric]) return scaleCache[metric];
        const idx = metric === "sol" ? 0 : 1;
        const all = [];
        for (const id in ledger.regions) {
          const ser = ledger.regions[id].series;
          for (const m in ser) { const v = ser[m][idx]; if (v > 0) all.push(v); }
        }
        all.sort(d3.ascending);
        const top = d3.quantile(all, 0.995) ?? 1;
        return (scaleCache[metric] = { top, hi: Math.log10(top + 1), n: all.length });
      };
      // inject normalized shade value v ∈ [0,1] into feature properties
      const shade = (month, metric) => {
        const vals = values(month, metric);
        const { hi } = scaleFor(metric);
        for (const f of geo.features) {
          const v = vals.get(f.properties.id) ?? 0;
          f.properties.v = Math.min(Math.log10(v + 1) / hi, 1);
        }
      };
      const tip = document.getElementById("tooltip");
      const panel = document.getElementById("region-panel");
      const tipHTML = (id) => {
        const reg = ledger.regions[id];
        const s = reg?.series[state.month];
        return `<b>${reg?.name ?? "—"}</b><br>${s ? `SOL ${s[0].toLocaleString()} · mean ${s[1]}` : "no data this month"}`;
      };
      function syncHash() {
        history.replaceState(null, "", `#m=${state.month}&x=${state.metric}${state.region ? `&r=${state.region}` : ""}`);
      }
      function openPanel(id) {
        const reg = ledger.regions[id];
        if (!reg) return;
        state.region = id;
        panel.hidden = false;
        document.getElementById("panel-name").textContent = reg.name;
        document.getElementById("panel-bps").textContent = `BPS ${reg.bps}`;
        const s = reg.series[state.month];
        document.getElementById("panel-sol").textContent = s ? s[0].toLocaleString() : "—";
        document.getElementById("panel-mean").textContent = s ? `${s[1]} nW/cm²·sr` : "—";
        document.getElementById("panel-months").textContent =
          `${Object.keys(reg.series).length} MONTHS IN LEDGER`;
        const spark = d3.select("#panel-spark").html("");
        const pts = ledger.months.map((m) => ({ m, v: reg.series[m]?.[0] ?? null }));
        const W = 240, H = 56;
        const x = d3.scalePoint(ledger.months, [4, W - 4]).padding(0.5);
        const y = d3.scaleLinear([0, d3.max(pts, (d) => d.v) || 1], [H - 6, 6]);
        const svg = spark.append("svg").attr("width", W).attr("height", H);
        svg.selectAll("circle").data(pts.filter((d) => d.v != null)).join("circle")
          .attr("cx", (d) => x(d.m)).attr("cy", (d) => y(d.v))
          .attr("r", (d) => (d.m === state.month ? 4 : 2.5))
          .attr("fill", (d) => (d.m === state.month ? "#FFEFC9" : "#E8A33D"));
        syncHash();
      }
      document.getElementById("panel-close").onclick = () => { panel.hidden = true; state.region = null; syncHash(); };

      function webglMap() {
      const map = new maplibregl.Map({
        container: "map",
        style: { version: 8, sources: {}, layers: [
          { id: "bg", type: "background", paint: { "background-color": "#05070F" } } ] },
        bounds: [[94.5, -11.5], [141.5, 6.5]],
        fitBoundsOptions: { padding: 24 },
        attributionControl: false,
        dragRotate: false,
      });
      map.addControl(new maplibregl.AttributionControl({
        customAttribution: "NASA Black Marble · geoBoundaries CC BY 3.0 IGO", compact: true }));
      map.addControl(new maplibregl.NavigationControl({ showCompass: false }));

      map.on("load", () => {
        shade(state.month, state.metric);
        map.addSource("regencies", { type: "geojson", data: geo, promoteId: "id" });
        map.addLayer({ id: "fill", type: "fill", source: "regencies",
          paint: { "fill-color": ["interpolate", ["linear"], ["get", "v"],
            0, RAMP[0], 0.25, RAMP[1], 0.5, RAMP[2], 0.75, RAMP[3], 1, RAMP[4]],
            "fill-opacity": 0.92 } });
        map.addLayer({ id: "line", type: "line", source: "regencies",
          paint: { "line-color": "#232B44", "line-width": 0.4 } });
        map.addLayer({ id: "hover", type: "line", source: "regencies",
          paint: { "line-color": "#E8A33D", "line-width": 1.4 },
          filter: ["==", ["get", "id"], ""] });
      });

      /* tooltip + click panel */
      map.on("mousemove", "fill", (e) => {
        const f = e.features[0];
        map.setFilter("hover", ["==", ["get", "id"], f.properties.id]);
        map.getCanvas().style.cursor = "pointer";
        tip.hidden = false;
        tip.style.left = e.point.x + 14 + "px";
        tip.style.top = e.point.y + 14 + "px";
        tip.innerHTML = tipHTML(f.properties.id);
      });
      map.on("mouseleave", "fill", () => {
        map.setFilter("hover", ["==", ["get", "id"], ""]);
        map.getCanvas().style.cursor = ""; tip.hidden = true;
      });
      map.on("click", "fill", (e) => openPanel(e.features[0].properties.id));
      return {
        paint(month, metric) { shade(month, metric); map.getSource("regencies")?.setData(geo); },
        ready(cb) { map.on("load", cb); },
      };
      }

      /* 2-D canvas choropleth — full function without WebGL (GPU acceleration off) */
      function canvasMap() {
        const container = document.getElementById("map");
        container.innerHTML = "";
        container.style.position = "relative";
        const canvas = document.createElement("canvas");
        canvas.style.cssText = "width:100%;height:100%;display:block;cursor:pointer;";
        container.appendChild(canvas);
        const note = document.createElement("div");
        note.style.cssText = "position:absolute;left:12px;top:10px;font-family:var(--font-data);font-size: 0.75rem;letter-spacing:0.08em;color:var(--ink-muted);";
        note.textContent = "2-D MAP (BROWSER GPU OFF) · NASA BLACK MARBLE · GEOBOUNDARIES CC BY 3.0 IGO";
        container.appendChild(note);
        const ctx = canvas.getContext("2d");
        const hitCtx = document.createElement("canvas").getContext("2d"); // identity-transform ctx for isPointInPath
        const dpr = Math.min(devicePixelRatio || 1, 2);
        const B = { w: 94.5, s: -11.5, e: 141.5, n: 6.5 };
        let W, H, sx, sy, ox, oy, paths = [], boxes = [];
        const ramp = d3.piecewise(d3.interpolateRgb, RAMP);
        function project() {
          W = container.clientWidth; H = container.clientHeight;
          canvas.width = W * dpr; canvas.height = H * dpr; ctx.setTransform(dpr, 0, 0, dpr, 0, 0);
          // isPointInPath returns false outside the canvas bitmap — size the hit-test canvas to match
          hitCtx.canvas.width = W; hitCtx.canvas.height = H;
          const pad = 20;
          const k = Math.min((W - 2 * pad) / (B.e - B.w), (H - 2 * pad) / (B.n - B.s));
          sx = k; sy = -k;
          ox = (W - k * (B.e - B.w)) / 2; oy = (H + k * (B.n - B.s)) / 2;
          paths = []; boxes = [];
          for (const f of geo.features) {
            const p = new Path2D();
            let x0 = Infinity, y0 = Infinity, x1 = -Infinity, y1 = -Infinity;
            const polys = f.geometry.type === "Polygon" ? [f.geometry.coordinates] : f.geometry.coordinates;
            for (const poly of polys) for (const ring of poly) {
              ring.forEach(([lon, lat], j) => {
                const px = ox + (lon - B.w) * sx, py = oy + (lat - B.s) * sy;
                if (px < x0) x0 = px; if (px > x1) x1 = px;
                if (py < y0) y0 = py; if (py > y1) y1 = py;
                j ? p.lineTo(px, py) : p.moveTo(px, py);
              });
              p.closePath();
            }
            paths.push(p); boxes.push([x0, y0, x1, y1]);
          }
        }
        let hoverIdx = -1;
        function paintAll() {
          ctx.fillStyle = "#05070F"; ctx.fillRect(0, 0, W, H);
          geo.features.forEach((f, i) => {
            ctx.fillStyle = ramp(f.properties.v ?? 0);
            ctx.fill(paths[i]);
            ctx.strokeStyle = "#232B44"; ctx.lineWidth = 0.4; ctx.stroke(paths[i]);
          });
          if (hoverIdx >= 0) { ctx.strokeStyle = "#E8A33D"; ctx.lineWidth = 1.4; ctx.stroke(paths[hoverIdx]); }
        }
        project();
        addEventListener("resize", () => { project(); paintAll(); });
        const featureAt = (e) => {
          // exact geometric hit test: bbox pre-filter, then point-in-polygon;
          // last (topmost-painted) match wins on any overlap
          const r = canvas.getBoundingClientRect();
          const px = e.clientX - r.left, py = e.clientY - r.top;
          for (let i = paths.length - 1; i >= 0; i--) {
            const b = boxes[i];
            if (px < b[0] || px > b[2] || py < b[1] || py > b[3]) continue;
            if (hitCtx.isPointInPath(paths[i], px, py)) return i;
          }
          return -1;
        };
        canvas.addEventListener("mousemove", (e) => {
          const i = featureAt(e);
          if (i !== hoverIdx) { hoverIdx = i; paintAll(); }
          if (i >= 0) {
            const r = canvas.getBoundingClientRect();
            tip.hidden = false;
            tip.style.left = e.clientX - r.left + 14 + "px";
            tip.style.top = e.clientY - r.top + 14 + "px";
            tip.innerHTML = tipHTML(geo.features[i].properties.id);
          } else tip.hidden = true;
        });
        canvas.addEventListener("mouseleave", () => { hoverIdx = -1; tip.hidden = true; paintAll(); });
        canvas.addEventListener("click", (e) => {
          const i = featureAt(e);
          if (i >= 0) openPanel(geo.features[i].properties.id);
        });
        // debug hook (harmless in production; lets tooling test the hit logic directly)
        window.__map2d = {
          n: () => paths.length,
          at: (px, py) => {
            for (let i = paths.length - 1; i >= 0; i--) {
              const b = boxes[i];
              if (px < b[0] || px > b[2] || py < b[1] || py > b[3]) continue;
              if (hitCtx.isPointInPath(paths[i], px, py)) return geo.features[i].properties.id;
            }
            return null;
          },
          box: (i) => boxes[i],
          probeDeep: (px, py) => {
            const cands = [];
            for (let i = 0; i < paths.length; i++) {
              const b = boxes[i];
              if (px >= b[0] && px <= b[2] && py >= b[1] && py <= b[3]) cands.push(i);
            }
            const results = cands.slice(0, 6).map((i) => ({
              i, id: geo.features[i].properties.id.slice(-6),
              hit: hitCtx.isPointInPath(paths[i], px, py),
              hitEvenOdd: hitCtx.isPointInPath(paths[i], px, py, "evenodd"),
              mainCtxHit: ctx.isPointInPath(paths[i], px / dpr, py / dpr),
            }));
            // self-test: first candidate's first vertex nudged inward
            return { hitW: hitCtx.canvas.width, hitH: hitCtx.canvas.height, dpr,
                     nCands: cands.length, results };
          },
        };
        return {
          paint(month, metric) { shade(month, metric); paintAll(); },
          ready(cb) { cb(); },
        };
      }

      let mapApi;
      try { mapApi = webglMap(); }
      catch (err) {
        console.warn("WebGL map unavailable — 2-D canvas fallback:", err?.message ?? err);
        mapApi = sect("map (2-D fallback)", () => canvasMap());
      }
      /* Legend ticks are the inverse of the shade transform, so they read in real
         units: v = log10(x+1)/hi  =>  x = 10^(v·hi) − 1. */
      const legendTitle = document.getElementById("legend-title");
      const legendTicks = document.getElementById("legend-ticks");
      function renderLegend() {
        if (!legendTicks) return;
        const { hi } = scaleFor(state.metric);
        const sol = state.metric === "sol";
        legendTitle.textContent = sol
          ? "TOTAL LIGHT · SUM OF RADIANCE PER REGENCY"
          : "INTENSITY · MEAN RADIANCE (nW/cm²·sr)";
        const f = sol ? d3.format(".2~s") : d3.format(".2~r");
        legendTicks.innerHTML = [0, 0.25, 0.5, 0.75, 1]
          .map((v) => `<span>${f(Math.pow(10, v * hi) - 1)}</span>`).join("");
      }
      renderLegend();
      if (mapApi) mapApi.ready(() => mapApi.paint(state.month, state.metric));

      /* controls + URL state (options already populated above) */
      const sel = document.getElementById("month-select");
      const bSol = document.getElementById("btn-sol"), bMean = document.getElementById("btn-mean");
      const setMetric = (metric) => {
        state.metric = metric;
        bSol.classList.toggle("on", metric === "sol");
        bMean.classList.toggle("on", metric === "mean");
        renderLegend();
        mapApi?.paint(state.month, state.metric); syncHash();
      };
      bSol.onclick = () => setMetric("sol");
      bMean.onclick = () => setMetric("mean");
      // restore state from URL
      const h = new URLSearchParams(location.hash.slice(1));
      if (h.get("m") && ledger.months.includes(h.get("m"))) { state.month = h.get("m"); sel.value = state.month; }
      if (h.get("x") === "mean") setMetric("mean");
      if (h.get("r")) mapApi?.ready(() => openPanel(h.get("r")));

      /* month-player: scrub or play the whole ledger as a timelapse */
      const months = ledger.months;
      const range = document.getElementById("month-range");
      const btnPlay = document.getElementById("btn-play");
      const hud = { month: document.getElementById("hud-month"), sol: document.getElementById("hud-sol"),
                    cov: document.getElementById("hud-cov"), mover: document.getElementById("hud-mover") };
      range.max = months.length - 1;
      const fmtSol = d3.format(".3~s"), fmtPct = d3.format(".0%");
      // largest year-on-year change in mean radiance among regencies that are ≥80% observed
      // in both months — sum-of-lights would move with cloud masking, mean moves with light
      const topMover = (m) => {
        const i = months.indexOf(m), j = i - 12;
        if (j < 0) return null;
        const floor = 0.001 * national[j].sol;
        let best = null;
        for (const id in ledger.regions) {
          const a = ledger.regions[id].series[m], b = ledger.regions[id].series[months[j]];
          if (!a || !b || b[0] < floor || b[1] <= 0 || a[2] < 0.8 * regionPeakPx[id] || b[2] < 0.8 * regionPeakPx[id]) continue;
          const d = a[1] / b[1] - 1;
          if (!best || Math.abs(d) > Math.abs(best.d)) best = { id, d };
        }
        return best;
      };
      function renderHUD(m) {
        const i = months.indexOf(m), n = national[i], cov = n.px / peakPx;
        hud.month.textContent = m;
        hud.sol.innerHTML = `SUM OF LIGHTS <b>${fmtSol(n.sol)}</b>`;
        const flag = cov < 0.02 ? "NO COMPOSITE" : cov < 0.5 ? "MONSOON-MASKED" : "";
        hud.cov.innerHTML = `COVERAGE <b>${fmtPct(cov)}</b>${flag ? ` <span class="masked">${flag}</span>` : ""}`;
        const mv = topMover(m);
        hud.mover.innerHTML = mv
          ? `TOP MOVER (YOY, MEAN) <b class="mover">${ledger.regions[mv.id].name}</b> ${mv.d >= 0 ? "+" : "−"}${fmtPct(Math.abs(mv.d))}`
          : "";
        range.value = i;
        range.style.setProperty("--pct", `${(i / Math.max(1, months.length - 1)) * 100}%`);
        sel.value = m;
      }
      function setMonth(m) {
        state.month = m;
        renderHUD(m);
        mapApi?.paint(state.month, state.metric);
        if (state.region) openPanel(state.region);
        syncHash();
      }
      let timer = null;
      const stop = () => { clearInterval(timer); timer = null; btnPlay.textContent = "▶"; btnPlay.setAttribute("aria-label", "play"); };
      const play = () => {
        let i = months.indexOf(state.month);
        if (i >= months.length - 1) i = -1;
        btnPlay.textContent = "❚❚"; btnPlay.setAttribute("aria-label", "pause");
        timer = setInterval(() => { i += 1; setMonth(months[i]); if (i >= months.length - 1) stop(); }, 650);
      };
      btnPlay.onclick = () => (timer ? stop() : play());
      range.oninput = () => setMonth(months[+range.value]);
      sel.onchange = () => setMonth(sel.value);
      renderHUD(state.month);
    </script>

    <script>
      /* ---------- 04 · Calibration — self-contained module (model stage) ---------- */
      import * as d3 from "d3";

      const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, "");
      const AMBER = "#E8A33D", TEAL = "#4BB8A9", SLATE = "#6B7CA6", INKMUT = "#9C9A8D";
      const failBanner = (msg) => {
        let b = document.getElementById("err-banner");
        if (!b) {
          b = document.createElement("div"); b.id = "err-banner";
          b.style.cssText = "position:fixed;bottom:0;left:0;right:0;z-index:99;background:#3A1E1A;color:#F26D5B;font:12px ui-monospace,monospace;padding:10px 16px;border-top:1px solid #F26D5B;";
          document.body.appendChild(b);
        }
        b.textContent = "⚠ " + msg;
      };
      const sect = (name, fn) => { try { return fn(); } catch (err) { console.error(name, err); failBanner(`${name} failed: ${err.message ?? err}`); return null; } };
      const $ = (id) => document.getElementById(id);
      const esc = (s) => String(s).replace(/[&<>"]/g, (c) => ({ "&": "&amp;", "<": "&lt;", ">": "&gt;", '"': "&quot;" }[c]));
      const ctip = $("calib-tip");
      const showTip = (e, html) => { ctip.hidden = false; ctip.innerHTML = html; ctip.style.left = e.pageX + 14 + "px"; ctip.style.top = e.pageY + 14 + "px"; };
      const hideTip = () => { ctip.hidden = true; };
      const pct1 = d3.format("+.1%"), pct0 = d3.format("+.0%"), pctu = d3.format(".1%"), fmtN = d3.format(",.0f");
      const MONTHS_EN = ["Jan", "Feb", "Mar", "Apr", "May", "Jun", "Jul", "Aug", "Sep", "Oct", "Nov", "Dec"];
      const pretty = (m) => `${MONTHS_EN[+m.slice(5) - 1]} ${m.slice(0, 4)}`;

      let cal = null;
      try {
        const res = await fetch(`${base}/data/calibration.json`);
        if (res.ok) cal = await res.json();
      } catch { /* pending note stays */ }

      if (cal) {
        $("calib-pending").hidden = true;
        for (const id of ["calib-tiles", "calib-pulse-block", "calib-scatter-block", "calib-flares-block"]) $(id).hidden = false;
        sect("calibration tiles", tiles);
        sect("growth chart", growthChart);
        sect("calibration scatter", scatterChart);
        sect("flare note", flareNote);
      }

      function tiles() {
        const r2s = cal.levels.map((d) => d.r2);
        const gate = cal.gates["G-A1"];
        const fe = cal.panel.annual_fe_regency, feW = cal.panel.annual_fe_regency_wellobs;
        const g = cal.growth.quarterly_yoy, h = cal.nowcast.headline;
        $("t-gate-v").innerHTML = `R² ${d3.min(r2s).toFixed(2)}–${d3.max(r2s).toFixed(2)} <span class="${gate.pass ? "pass" : "fail"}">${gate.pass ? "PASS" : "FAIL"}</span>`;
        $("t-gate-s").textContent = `log PDRB ~ log lights, ${cal.bps.n_regencies} regencies, every year ${cal.levels[0].year}–${cal.levels.at(-1).year} · gate ≥ ${gate.threshold}`;
        $("t-el-v").textContent = fe.beta.toFixed(2);
        $("t-el-s").textContent = `± ${(1.96 * fe.se).toFixed(2)} (95%, clustered) · doubling lights ↔ ${pct0(2 ** fe.beta - 1)} PDRB · rises to ${feW.beta.toFixed(2)} on well-observed years`;
        $("t-gr-v").textContent = `β ${g.beta.toFixed(3)}`;
        $("t-gr-s").textContent = `quarterly YoY growth on growth, R² ${g.r2.toFixed(2)} — lights say where, hardly when; the bands stay honest`;
        /* Withdrawn after review: with beta this small the headline is almost
           entirely the intercept, so we publish that share instead of the forecast. */
        const contrib = g.beta * h.lights_growth;
        const constShare = 1 - Math.abs(contrib) / h.g;
        const oosA = cal.oos?.annual;
        $("t-nc-v").textContent = `${pctu(constShare)} constant`;
        $("t-nc-s").textContent =
          `national lights moved ${pct1(h.lights_growth)} and contributed ${(contrib * 100).toFixed(3)} pp ` +
          `to a ${pct1(h.g)} headline · band ${((h.hi - h.lo) * 100).toFixed(2)} pp, ` +
          `${((h.hi - h.lo) / Math.abs(contrib)).toFixed(0)}× the signal` +
          (oosA ? ` · out of sample ${Math.round((oosA.mae_lights / oosA.mae_naive - 1) * 100)}% worse than naive` : "");
      }

      function growthChart() {
        const el = $("calib-pulse");
        const S = cal.nowcast.series;
        const W = el.clientWidth, H = 320, M = { t: 18, r: 20, b: 30, l: 56 };
        const months = S.map((d) => d.m);
        const x = d3.scalePoint(months, [M.l, W - M.r]);
        const years = [...new Set(months.map((m) => m.slice(0, 4)))];
        const annual = cal.nowcast.bps_annual.filter((a) => years.includes(String(a.year)));
        const quarterly = cal.nowcast.bps_quarterly
          .map((q) => ({ ...q, m: `${q.year}-${String(q.quarter * 3).padStart(2, "0")}` }))
          .filter((q) => months.includes(q.m));
        const lo = Math.min(d3.min(S, (d) => d.lo), d3.min(annual, (d) => d.g) ?? 0, 0) - 0.005;
        const hi = Math.max(d3.max(S, (d) => d.hi), d3.max(annual, (d) => d.g) ?? 0) + 0.016;
        const y = d3.scaleLinear([lo, hi], [H - M.b, M.t]);
        const svg = d3.select(el).append("svg").attr("width", W).attr("height", H);

        // nowcast zone — months beyond the last BPS quarter
        const firstNow = S.find((d) => d.nowcast);
        if (firstNow) {
          svg.append("rect").attr("x", x(firstNow.m) - x.step() / 2).attr("y", M.t)
            .attr("width", W - M.r - x(firstNow.m) + x.step() / 2).attr("height", H - M.t - M.b)
            .attr("fill", "#E9E4D6").attr("opacity", 0.045);
          svg.append("text").attr("x", W - M.r - 4).attr("y", M.t + 12).attr("text-anchor", "end")
            .attr("class", "annot").text("NOWCAST — BPS NOT YET PUBLISHED");
        }
        svg.append("g").attr("transform", `translate(${M.l},0)`).attr("class", "axis")
          .call(d3.axisLeft(y).ticks(6).tickFormat(pct0));
        svg.append("g").attr("transform", `translate(0,${H - M.b})`).attr("class", "axis")
          .call(d3.axisBottom(x).tickValues(months.filter((m) => m.endsWith("-01"))).tickFormat((m) => m.slice(0, 4)));
        if (lo < 0) svg.append("line").attr("x1", M.l).attr("x2", W - M.r).attr("y1", y(0)).attr("y2", y(0))
          .attr("stroke", "#E9E4D6").attr("stroke-opacity", 0.25);

        // COVID annotation
        if (months.includes("2020-06")) {
          svg.append("line").attr("x1", x("2020-06")).attr("x2", x("2020-06")).attr("y1", M.t).attr("y2", H - M.b)
            .attr("stroke", "#3A4452").attr("stroke-dasharray", "3 4");
          svg.append("text").attr("x", x("2020-06") + 5).attr("y", M.t + 12).attr("class", "annot")
            .text("2020 · COVID — lights and GDP both fell ~2%, but coverage fell too");
        }

        svg.append("path").datum(S)
          .attr("d", d3.area().x((d) => x(d.m)).y0((d) => y(d.lo)).y1((d) => y(d.hi)))
          .attr("fill", AMBER).attr("opacity", 0.14);
        svg.append("path").datum(S)
          .attr("d", d3.line().x((d) => x(d.m)).y((d) => y(d.g)))
          .attr("fill", "none").attr("stroke", AMBER).attr("stroke-width", 2).attr("stroke-linejoin", "round");
        for (const a of annual) {
          const ms = months.filter((m) => m.startsWith(String(a.year)));
          if (!ms.length) continue;
          svg.append("line").attr("x1", x(ms[0])).attr("x2", x(ms.at(-1))).attr("y1", y(a.g)).attr("y2", y(a.g))
            .attr("stroke", TEAL).attr("stroke-width", 2);
        }
        svg.selectAll("circle.q").data(quarterly).join("circle").attr("class", "q")
          .attr("cx", (d) => x(d.m)).attr("cy", (d) => y(d.g)).attr("r", 4.5)
          .attr("fill", TEAL).attr("stroke", "#0A0E1A").attr("stroke-width", 2);

        // end label on the lights-implied line
        const last = S.at(-1);
        svg.append("text").attr("x", x(last.m) - 6).attr("y", y(last.lo) + 16).attr("text-anchor", "end")
          .attr("class", "annot").attr("fill", "#E9E4D6").text(`lights-implied ${pct1(last.g)}`);

        // hover: crosshair + one tooltip, every series
        const guide = svg.append("line").attr("y1", M.t).attr("y2", H - M.b)
          .attr("stroke", "#E9E4D6").attr("stroke-opacity", 0.4).style("display", "none");
        const dot = svg.append("circle").attr("r", 4.5).attr("fill", AMBER).attr("stroke", "#0A0E1A")
          .attr("stroke-width", 2).style("display", "none");
        svg.append("rect").attr("x", M.l).attr("y", M.t).attr("width", W - M.l - M.r).attr("height", H - M.t - M.b)
          .attr("fill", "transparent")
          .on("mousemove", (e) => {
            const px = d3.pointer(e)[0];
            const d = S.reduce((b, s) => (Math.abs(x(s.m) - px) < Math.abs(x(b.m) - px) ? s : b), S[0]);
            guide.style("display", null).attr("x1", x(d.m)).attr("x2", x(d.m));
            dot.style("display", null).attr("cx", x(d.m)).attr("cy", y(d.g));
            const a = annual.find((v) => String(v.year) === d.m.slice(0, 4));
            const q = quarterly.find((v) => v.year === +d.m.slice(0, 4) && v.quarter === Math.ceil(+d.m.slice(5) / 3));
            showTip(e, `<b>${pretty(d.m)}</b>${d.nowcast ? " · <span style='color:#E8A33D'>NOWCAST</span>" : ""}<br>` +
              `<span style="color:${AMBER}">—</span> lights-implied <b>${pct1(d.g)}</b> <span style="color:${INKMUT}">[${pct1(d.lo)} … ${pct1(d.hi)}]</span><br>` +
              `<span style="color:${INKMUT}">deseasonalised lights YoY ${pct0(d.gl)} · coverage ${pctu(d.cov)}</span><br>` +
              `<span style="color:${TEAL}">—</span> BPS ${d.m.slice(0, 4)} annual ${a ? `<b>${pct1(a.g)}</b>` : "not yet published"}` +
              (q ? `<br><span style="color:${TEAL}">●</span> BPS ${q.q} <b>${pct1(q.g)}</b>` : ""));
          })
          .on("mouseleave", () => { guide.style("display", "none"); dot.style("display", "none"); hideTip(); });
      }

      function scatterChart() {
        const el = $("calib-scatter");
        const years = cal.scatter.years, pts = cal.scatter.points;
        const lv = Object.fromEntries(cal.levels.map((d) => [d.year, d]));
        const gate = cal.gates["G-A1"];
        $("sc-gate").textContent = `${gate.pass ? "PASS" : "FAIL"} · min R² ${gate.min_r2.toFixed(2)}`;
        $("sc-gate").classList.add(gate.pass ? "pass" : "fail");
        let yi = years.length - 1;
        const W = Math.max(el.clientWidth, 320), H = 360, M = { t: 14, r: 16, b: 40, l: 58 };
        const finite = (a) => a.filter((v) => v != null && isFinite(v));
        const xd = d3.extent(pts.flatMap((p) => finite(p.x))), yd = d3.extent(pts.flatMap((p) => finite(p.y)));
        const X = d3.scaleLinear(xd, [M.l, W - M.r]).nice();
        const Y = d3.scaleLinear(yd, [H - M.b, M.t]).nice();
        const lnTicks = (sc) => {
          const [a, b] = sc.domain(), out = [];
          for (let k = Math.ceil(a / Math.LN10); k * Math.LN10 <= b; k++) out.push(k * Math.LN10);
          return out;
        };
        const svg = d3.select(el).append("svg").attr("width", W).attr("height", H);
        svg.append("g").attr("transform", `translate(0,${H - M.b})`).attr("class", "axis")
          .call(d3.axisBottom(X).tickValues(lnTicks(X)).tickFormat((v) => d3.format("~s")(Math.round(Math.exp(v)))));
        svg.append("g").attr("transform", `translate(${M.l},0)`).attr("class", "axis")
          .call(d3.axisLeft(Y).tickValues(lnTicks(Y)).tickFormat((v) => d3.format("~s")(Math.round(Math.exp(v)))));
        svg.append("text").attr("class", "annot").attr("x", (M.l + W - M.r) / 2).attr("y", H - 6)
          .attr("text-anchor", "middle").text("SUM OF LIGHTS, SEASONALLY ADJUSTED (LOG SCALE)");
        svg.append("text").attr("class", "annot").attr("transform", `translate(12,${(M.t + H - M.b) / 2}) rotate(-90)`)
          .attr("text-anchor", "middle").text("REAL PDRB, BN RP (LOG SCALE)");

        const fit = svg.append("line").attr("stroke", TEAL).attr("stroke-width", 2);
        const dots = svg.selectAll("circle.p").data(pts).join("circle").attr("class", "p")
          .attr("r", 3)
          .attr("fill", (p) => (p.flare ? "transparent" : AMBER))
          .attr("stroke", AMBER).attr("stroke-width", (p) => (p.flare ? 1.2 : 0))
          .attr("opacity", 0.55);
        const hover = svg.append("circle").attr("r", 6).attr("fill", "none")
          .attr("stroke", "#E9E4D6").attr("stroke-width", 1.5).style("display", "none");

        let del = null;
        function draw(animate) {
          const l = lv[years[yi]];
          $("sc-r2").textContent = `R² ${l.r2.toFixed(3)} · slope ${l.slope.toFixed(2)} · n ${l.n}`;
          d3.select("#sc-years").selectAll("button").attr("class", (d, i) => (i === yi ? "on" : null));
          const sel = animate ? dots.transition().duration(500).ease(d3.easeCubicOut) : dots;
          sel.attr("cx", (p) => X(p.x[yi] ?? xd[0]))
             .attr("cy", (p) => Y(p.y[yi] ?? yd[0]))
             .attr("display", (p) => (p.x[yi] == null || p.y[yi] == null ? "none" : null));
          const [a, b] = X.domain();
          const fy = (v) => Y(l.intercept + l.slope * v);
          const ft = animate ? fit.transition().duration(500) : fit;
          ft.attr("x1", X(a)).attr("y1", fy(a)).attr("x2", X(b)).attr("y2", fy(b));
          del = d3.Delaunay.from(pts, (p) => (p.x[yi] == null ? -1e4 : X(p.x[yi])), (p) => (p.y[yi] == null ? -1e4 : Y(p.y[yi])));
        }
        for (const [i, yr] of years.entries()) {
          const b = document.createElement("button");
          b.textContent = yr;
          b.onclick = () => { yi = i; draw(true); };
          $("sc-years").appendChild(b);
        }
        draw(false);

        svg.append("rect").attr("x", M.l).attr("y", M.t).attr("width", W - M.l - M.r).attr("height", H - M.t - M.b)
          .attr("fill", "transparent")
          .on("mousemove", (e) => {
            const [mx, my] = d3.pointer(e);
            const i = del.find(mx, my);
            const p = pts[i];
            if (!p || p.x[yi] == null || Math.hypot(X(p.x[yi]) - mx, Y(p.y[yi]) - my) > 28) { hover.style("display", "none"); hideTip(); return; }
            hover.style("display", null).attr("cx", X(p.x[yi])).attr("cy", Y(p.y[yi]));
            showTip(e, `<b>${esc(p.name)}</b><br>real PDRB <b>Rp ${fmtN(Math.exp(p.y[yi]))} bn</b> · lights ${fmtN(Math.exp(p.x[yi]))}<br>` +
              `<span style="color:${INKMUT}">residual ${p.sr[yi] != null ? `${p.sr[yi] > 0 ? "+" : ""}${p.sr[yi].toFixed(1)}σ` : "—"}` +
              `${p.flare ? " · flare-corrected" : ""} · ${years[yi]}</span>`);
          })
          .on("mouseleave", () => { hover.style("display", "none"); hideTip(); });

        // weak-fit list
        $("wk-title").textContent = `WHERE SATELLITE AND STATISTICS DISAGREE · ${cal.weakFit.year}`;
        const ol = $("calib-weak");
        for (const w of cal.weakFit.list.slice(0, 8)) {
          const li = document.createElement("li");
          const name = document.createElement("span");
          name.textContent = w.name;
          if (w.tags?.length) {
            const t = document.createElement("span"); t.className = "tags"; t.textContent = w.tags.join(" · ");
            name.appendChild(t);
          }
          const sig = document.createElement("span"); sig.className = "sig";
          sig.textContent = `${w.std_resid > 0 ? "+" : ""}${w.std_resid.toFixed(1)}σ`;
          li.append(name, sig);
          ol.appendChild(li);
        }
      }

      function flareNote() {
        const f = cal.flares;
        if (!f) { $("calib-flares-block").hidden = true; return; }
        $("calib-flares-note").innerHTML =
          `Gas flares are light without economy underneath. <b>${f.n_sites} persistent flare sites</b> ` +
          `(seen in ≥${f.min_survey_years} of 8 annual surveys) are buffered at <b>${f.buffer_km}&nbsp;km</b> — the measured glow radius; ` +
          `the spec’s 5&nbsp;km would swallow whole towns — and each regency’s series is corrected by its share of light inside the buffers, ` +
          `year by year, before deseasonalisation. Nationally that removes <b>${pctu(f.national_share)}</b> of all light in ${f.year} ` +
          `(5&nbsp;km: ${pctu(f.national_share_5km)}; 1.5&nbsp;km: ${pctu(f.national_share_15km)}). The raw series is kept. ` +
          `Sites first lit after 2019 are not in the survey — a known limit, stated here.`;
        const max = f.regencies[0]?.share ?? 1;
        const ol = $("calib-flares");
        for (const r of f.regencies.slice(0, 8)) {
          const li = document.createElement("li");
          li.innerHTML = `<span class="rname">${esc(r.name)}</span>` +
            `<span class="rbar"><i style="width:${(r.share / max) * 100}%;background:${SLATE}"></i></span>` +
            `<span class="rval">−${pctu(r.share)}</span>`;
          li.title = `${r.sites} flare sites · 5 km buffer would take ${pctu(r.share_wide)}, 1.5 km ${pctu(r.share_tight)}`;
          ol.appendChild(li);
        }
        $("calib-flares-src").textContent =
          `Share of the regency's sum-of-lights removed, ${f.year} composite. Source: ${f.source}, doi:${f.doi} — ${f.licence}.`;
      }
    </script>

    <style is:global>
      html { scroll-behavior: smooth; }
      body { margin: 0; }
